{"kind":"report","text":"PB-1 plan is at /Users/hughpyle/play/dap-ui-sdk/PLAN-presence.md, SHA-256 2a510d81e53676b37ae1cb75748259b429267ebb2b13605bbcf4457f8feee43a. The files were inspected as working trees. Pinboard has no Git repository at its root and Foldkit has an unborn main ref, so this plan makes no commit or clean-state claim.\n\n1. Reuse Map’s live summary, signed-act and generation contracts, session fencing and watch invalidation pattern. Map uses a configured full live scope ref in app/entry.ts:37–39. Pinboard adapts viewport data, app grants, child discovery and per-tab identity. Both could share session-aware read/act scheduling, renewal, re-entry and teardown in the client.\n2. Propose one owned pinned live child per recorded board, with member plus tab discriminator, a bounded viewport and name, enter/update/leave and timed expiry. Use 128 nonfinal items, 120 seconds from the last commit, renewal every 25 seconds, and budget all retained finals until restart. A 120-second lease can retain a closed tab longer than today’s 30-second expiry.\n3. Use Pinboard’s existing real invitation and WebCrypto device enrollment before presence shares anything. Issue a session for the actual member and grant pinboard.presence under reviewed room policy. The unsigned name path remains local-only until it has authority and a verified child. A tab identifier permits separate rows for the same member and supplies no separate authorization.\n4. A new recorded board genesis creates and keeps the exact child ref. Existing boards need an explicit migration or a new install. Open one authenticated watch and reread on its events. Under Map’s cadence a single idle tab nominally performs 144 renewals, 144 pre-act reads and 144 own-change reads per hour, plus its watch and setup. Five tabs observing all changes conditionally total 5,040 calls plus watches. Measure real Worker requests and coalescing.\n5. Three separate dap findings. packages/client/src/application-gateway.ts:43–81 lacks live, live-act and live-stream in the maintained screen allowlist, while the room implements them. packages/client/src/handle.ts:111–124 exposes live summary and act but lacks the reusable typed watch and lifecycle that Map implements in its app. packages/platform/src/application-codec/application-view-binding.ts:100–108 and 118–121 fixes B4 member/focus uniqueness and the effect shapes, which cannot carry this tab and rectangle shape unchanged. The Pinboard local host’s missing child provisioning and authorization are app work.\n6. Witness two real members moving and resizing on one installed board, denial across signers, same-member tabs with separate rectangles, and a closed tab whose leave cannot arrive. Require removal within 120 seconds after close, record the last accepted expiry and visible delay, and test generation reset/re-entry and bounded refusal. The plan is the only file added."}